     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"direction:ltr;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">\r\nGeom raster is your best option. For such small array it works fine.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"direction:ltr;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">\r\nIn case you need something stronger for larger data simply use a KDE 2D estimate as quick and dirty solution to reduce the data set to information\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"direction:ltr;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"direction:ltr;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">\r\nGet <a href=\"https://aka.ms/ghei36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://aka.ms/ghei36&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373215000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26MboNVXtwqYz7u_CooKRm\">Outlook for Android</a></div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-size:11pt\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Kavee L &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xcub...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, December 14, 2018 12:32:02 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> ggplot2<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: Heatmaps</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Something like this ?\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<code>df <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span> read_csv<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;heatmap.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><br>\r\ndf <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">%&gt;%</span> gather<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span>value<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span>X1<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">%&gt;%</span> <br>\r\n       mutate<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">as</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span>integer<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">%&gt;%</span> <br>\r\n       ggplot<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>aes<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> y<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>X1<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> fill<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> value<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span> geom_raster<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span></code></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nIt is more efficient, right?</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thank you for the suggestion. (I&#39;m still a newbie)</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Best,</div>\r\n<div>Kavee<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOn Thursday, December 13, 2018 at 3:45:54 PM UTC-5, David Kahle wrote:\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Have you tried geom_raster()?\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>david.<br>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On Dec 13, 2018, at 1:40 PM, Kavee L &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">xcub...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>How about this (it is not an optimal solution):</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<code>\r\n<div><span><br>\r\ndf </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> read_csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;heatmap.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br>\r\ndf </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> gather</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span>X1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> <br>\r\n       mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>integer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> <br>\r\n       ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>X1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>\r\n color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n</code></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Best,</div>\r\n<div>Kavee<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><span>&lt;Rplot03.png&gt;</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><span>&lt;Rplot01.png&gt;</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOn Thursday, October 11, 2018 at 7:23:02 AM UTC-4, hfz.ali....@<a href=\"http://gmail.com\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1QXzXMxGGIlfFmi3FInCS7\">gmail.com</a> wrote:\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br>\r\nI am trying to plot heatmap with huge data matrix, can someone help me how I can construct heatmap similar to attached image.\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thanks</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2--YuywuZLsPxb-2Nl7Rdm\">\r\nhttps://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: <a rel=\"nofollow\">email ...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: <a rel=\"nofollow\">email ggplot...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38NDFkWWLLrVzvTptJf2-Z\">\r\nhttp://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggplot2&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw25-OPI-mUwImbPdQpAbAZB\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n<span>&lt;Rplot03.png&gt;</span><span>&lt;Rplot01.png&gt;</span></div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n===================================<br>\r\n<br>\r\nDavid J. Kahle, Ph.D.<br>\r\nAssociate Professor<br>\r\nDepartment of Statistical Science<br>\r\nBaylor University<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.kahle.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.kahle.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366373216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2cmPszT6JKGkDGrb-DmmVz\">www.kahle.io</a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible e